<title>USA: Alpharma gets baldness drug ok for women.</title>
<headline>Alpharma gets baldness drug ok for women.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LEE, N.J. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpharma Inc said Monday that its U.S. Pharmaceuticals Division received approval from the Food and Drug Administration to manufacture and market Minoxidil Topical Solution two percent for women.</p>
<p>Minoxidil is the generic equivalent of Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc's Rogaine.</p>
<p>Alpharma received FDA approval last year to manufacture and market Minoxidil Topical Solution for treatment of male pattern baldness, which it began distributing during the second quarter of 1996.</p>
</text>
